{"verdicts":[{"id":"X01","label":"incidental","mixed":true,"confidence":"high","justification":"Beginning with a place is chiefly a bureau or desk convention, though bureau-produced reporting may also benefit from genuine local expertise."},{"id":"X02","label":"quality_relevant","mixed":false,"confidence":"high","justification":"A promise of actionable help communicates substantive utility that can directly motivate readers to open the story."},{"id":"X03","label":"quality_relevant","mixed":false,"confidence":"medium","justification":"Making an unresolved cause central creates a substantive mystery and information need rather than merely marking a surface convention."},{"id":"X04","label":"quality_relevant","mixed":false,"confidence":"high","justification":"Explicit conflict between meaningful social or ideological positions is substantive information about the story's stakes."},{"id":"X05","label":"incidental","mixed":false,"confidence":"high","justification":"Counting geographic names primarily identifies foreign or location-oriented subject matter rather than a generally meaningful appeal property."},{"id":"X06","label":"incidental","mixed":false,"confidence":"high","justification":"A celebrity-name-and-colon opening combines a topic marker with desk and placement conventions."},{"id":"X07","label":"quality_relevant","mixed":false,"confidence":"high","justification":"Invoking belonging or a shared identity is substantive audience relevance that can genuinely shape reading interest."},{"id":"X08","label":"quality_relevant","mixed":false,"confidence":"high","justification":"A precise and honestly resolvable information gap is a substantive reason for readers to open and read the story."},{"id":"X09","label":"incidental","mixed":false,"confidence":"high","justification":"UK references chiefly mark domestic subject matter and a larger home-audience baseline."},{"id":"X10","label":"incidental","mixed":false,"confidence":"high","justification":"The presence of quotation marks alone is a punctuation and format fingerprint rather than evidence about substantive appeal."},{"id":"X11","label":"quality_relevant","mixed":false,"confidence":"high","justification":"Concrete, readily imagined scenes communicate the event more vividly and can substantively engage readers."},{"id":"X12","label":"incidental","mixed":true,"confidence":"high","justification":"This construction principally identifies a feature-commission format, although such commissions may also contain genuinely compelling personal reporting."},{"id":"X13","label":"incidental","mixed":true,"confidence":"medium","justification":"The mere presence of numbers can fingerprint data-led or breaking-news treatments, though those practices may also supply genuinely useful precision."},{"id":"X14","label":"incidental","mixed":true,"confidence":"medium","justification":"First-person wording primarily marks a testimonial or feature format, although that upstream reporting approach can also provide substantive human perspective."},{"id":"X15","label":"quality_relevant","mixed":false,"confidence":"high","justification":"Identifying evidence or attribution substantively clarifies the provenance and credibility of a claim."},{"id":"X16","label":"incidental","mixed":true,"confidence":"high","justification":"Reliance on prior knowledge is mainly a temporal running-story fingerprint, though major stories that receive follow-ups may also retain genuine reader interest."},{"id":"X17","label":"incidental","mixed":true,"confidence":"high","justification":"Stock recap wording fingerprints a later story position or explainer slot, although a real explainer can also offer substantive understanding."},{"id":"X18","label":"incidental","mixed":false,"confidence":"high","justification":"Ending with a question mark is purely a punctuation convention without establishing the question's substantive value."},{"id":"X19","label":"quality_relevant","mixed":false,"confidence":"high","justification":"When emotion is genuinely the story, naming it communicates substantive human stakes and affective relevance."},{"id":"X20","label":"quality_relevant","mixed":false,"confidence":"high","justification":"A clear consequence for the reader's money, health, rights, or daily life is direct substantive relevance."},{"id":"X21","label":"incidental","mixed":true,"confidence":"medium","justification":"Formulaic explainer labels chiefly mark an editorial format, although the associated analysis may also deliver genuinely useful understanding."},{"id":"X22","label":"quality_relevant","mixed":false,"confidence":"high","justification":"Withholding a salient answer creates a substantive information gap that can directly motivate a click."},{"id":"X23","label":"quality_relevant","mixed":false,"confidence":"high","justification":"Concrete effects on individual health, safety, rights, or routines are substantive personal stakes."},{"id":"X24","label":"incidental","mixed":false,"confidence":"high","justification":"Literal second-person token counts measure an addressing habit while explicitly ignoring whether the story truly affects the reader."},{"id":"X25","label":"incidental","mixed":false,"confidence":"high","justification":"Word count is a pure length property and does not assess whether the additional wording communicates anything useful."},{"id":"X26","label":"incidental","mixed":true,"confidence":"medium","justification":"Scare quotes are chiefly a punctuation and hedging convention, though an upstream practice of qualified attribution can sometimes improve accuracy."},{"id":"X27","label":"quality_relevant","mixed":false,"confidence":"high","justification":"An explicitly divisive proposition or conflict between camps is substantive information about the story's social stakes."},{"id":"X28","label":"quality_relevant","mixed":false,"confidence":"medium","justification":"The contrast between an ordinary relatable action and a remarkable outcome is a substantive human-interest hook."},{"id":"X29","label":"incidental","mixed":true,"confidence":"medium","justification":"Question-to-reader phrasing is largely a rhetorical template, although it may originate in genuinely informative service or explainer journalism."}]}
